# court_lib.haro -- the generic court of a declared language, in pure core Ring.
#
# A court FORGED from a .haro declaration is a generated program that loads
# this file and fills five tables (see forge.haro): the language's name and
# extension, its declaration kinds with their typed seats, its forms, and
# its declared refusal phrasings. Everything the DECLARATION says is judged
# here: the Commons' lexical form (C6), the DEFINE shape, the closed verb
# set, the closed clause set per kind, each clause's value shape, a clause
# given twice, a missing RATIONALE, a required seat absent, one namespace.
# What the declaration does NOT say -- a menu of words, a default, an order,
# a rule between two declarations -- is not judged here, and the guard
# counts those apart. That count is the spike's measurement.
#
# Phrasings follow harb's court (harobanda/src/machine.zig) for the shapes
# the Grammar Commons gives every court, so the fixtures' fragments can be
# compared; where the declaration carries a REFUSAL message, it is spoken.
#
# v0.2 (haro/spike/v02/GRAMMAR.md): a seat's type may be a MENU (a word of
# its WORDS), a RANGE (a number within it), a FORMAT (a text of its shape)
# or a DECLARATION (a reference that must resolve); a declaration's NAMES
# are drawn from a MENU or a FORMAT; the WORLD's ONE and FIRST hold; every
# CONSTRAINT's condition is evaluated on every declaration of its ON kind,
# and its MESSAGE is spoken with {name}, {seat}, {other} and {decl.seat}
# filled in. The refinement gate reads the REFINE's POINTS and FLOOR.
#
# v0.3 (haro/spike/v03/GRAMMAR.md): a UNION seat takes a value of one of
# several shapes and is checked as the alternative the shape names; a
# declaration's MESSAGES speak for its reference seats; a condition reads
# through a reference, quantifies, and tests the closed relations; and the
# order of the court is: shapes, the WORLD, the local types, the
# CONSTRAINTs, then the references.
#
# v0.17 (haro/spike/v17/GRAMMAR.md): UNDERSTAND -- a language that declares how a human language reaches its
# closed questions gets `tokens`, `understand`, `ask`, `vocabulary` and `examples`, and the rules of its
# sentences (n_lib.haro, loaded only by a court forged from such a language): `check <file> surfaces` asks each
# surface's own court to judge its queries too.
#
# v0.14 (haro/spike/v14/GRAMMAR.md): a court that collects -- `diagnose` goes on
# past a refusal to the next element of every pass and answers every finding,
# in the order of the file; `check` still stops at the first, to the byte.
#
# v0.13 (haro/spike/v13/GRAMMAR.md): NARRATE -- `narrate <file>` answers the
# sentence back in the language's own voice (narrate_lib.haro, loaded only where
# a NARRATE is declared): a projection of the sentence on stdout, never stored,
# never read back.
#
# v0.12 (haro/spike/v12/GRAMMAR.md): FORMS -- `family <file>` generates every
# declared family from its base and the forms it offers; `spellings <file>
# <names>` judges a list of names against the FORMS and the families
# (forms_lib.haro, loaded only where a FORMS is declared).
#
# v0.11 (haro/spike/v11/GRAMMAR.md): the Diagnostic Contract -- `diagnose
# <file> [world]` answers the court's verdict as C2 v1.2.0's one object of
# six-field envelopes; a typed refusal carries the declaration's CODE / CODES
# and CITES (CtFailC), a parse-level one is PARSE with no cites.
#
# v0.10 (haro/spike/v10/GRAMMAR.md): the WORLD as versioned data -- a SYMBOL
# seat resolves against a C1 world.json handed to `check <file> [world]`
# (UNRESOLVED in the symbol's words; NO_WORLD a warning without one), and
# `world <file>` emits the sentence's own C1 rows.
#
# v0.9 (haro/spike/v09/GRAMMAR.md): the RUN -- the A letter -- and the `run`
# verb: `run <file> <algorithm> <record json>` walks an algorithm's step tree
# on a record and answers its result (run_lib.haro, loaded by the generated
# court when its language declares a RUN); a step tree with a cycle is
# refused at check.
#
# v0.8 (haro/spike/v08/GRAMMAR.md): a refusal by NAME for a known trespasser;
# pair lists keyed by a MENU (a sequence) or a DECLARATION (resolved) with
# reference values; a UNION of declarations resolved by name; the references
# pass judges every reference, scalar, listed, keyed or valued.
#
# v0.7 (haro/spike/v07/GRAMMAR.md): the ASK -- the Q letter -- and the `ask`
# verb: `ask <file> "<question>" <rows json>` answers a question of the
# declared world on the records handed in (ask_lib.haro, loaded by the
# generated court when its language declares an ASK).
#
# v0.6 (haro/spike/v06/GRAMMAR.md): a list of a FORM that is a name and a
# scalar is written as name: value pairs; a seat typed by an EXPRESSION holds
# an expression text the court parses with the expression's own menus
# (expr_lib.haro); and the sentence court RUNS what the declaration says a
# record does -- `eval <file> <decl> <seat> <json>` evaluates one expression
# seat on a record, `walk <file> <name> <json>` walks the record through the
# steps the WALK of that kind names, in ORDER, under its GUARDS, computing
# its COMPUTE seats by their FORMULAs, stopping at the first guard that fails.
#
# Functions only. Globals ($cCourtLang, $cCourtExt, $aCourtKinds,
# $aCourtForms, $aCourtRefusals, $aCourtMenus, $aCourtRanges,
# $aCourtFormats, $aCourtUnions, $aCourtConstraints, $aCourtWorld,
# $aCourtPoints, $aCourtFloors, $aCourtToks, $nCourtPos, and cond_lib's)
# are born in the generated court, at its top level, for both runtimes' sake.

load "cond_lib.haro"
load "block_lib.haro"
# expr_lib.haro is loaded by the GENERATED court, and only when its language
# declares an EXPRESSION (forge.haro): a court carries what its language says,
# and the machine court's edit-to-verdict stays under its 100 ms target

# ---- character classes by byte code (HF-30) ---------------------------------

func CtIsDigit(tC)
	nN = Ascii(tC)
	return (nN >= 48 and nN <= 57)
end
func CtIsLowerish(tC)
	nN = Ascii(tC)
	return (nN >= 97 and nN <= 122) or nN = 95 or (nN >= 48 and nN <= 57)
end
func CtIsUpperish(tC)
	nN = Ascii(tC)
	return (nN >= 65 and nN <= 90) or nN = 95 or (nN >= 48 and nN <= 57)
end
func CtFail(nLine, tMsg)
	Raise($tCourtLang + " (line " + String(nLine) + "): " + tMsg)
end
# v0.11: a refusal that enforces a provision of the declaration -- the pinned
# instrument -- carries its code and its cites out through two globals the
# `diagnose` verb reads; a parse-level refusal leaves them at PARSE and [],
# which C2 2.5 calls honest. A code of PARSE never cites.
func CtFailC(nLine, tCode, xCites, tMsg)
	CtSetCode(tCode, xCites)
	CtFail(nLine, tMsg)
end
# v0.14: a collecting court. In collect mode a refusal that a pass meets at one
# of its raising sites is NOTED and the pass goes on to its next element; out
# of collect mode it is raised again, same string, same globals, so `check` is
# unchanged to the byte. A declaration whose clause has the wrong SHAPE is
# broken: the passes that read its values say nothing more about it.
func CtNote(tErr)
	if not $bCourtCollect Raise(tErr) end
	$vCourtFound + [$tCourtCode, $xCourtCites, CtLineOf(tErr), CtStripPrefix(tErr)]
	CtSetCode("PARSE", [])
end
func CtIsBroken(nDecl)
	for i = 1 to Len($vCourtBroken)
		if $vCourtBroken[i] = nDecl return true end
	end
	return false
end
# the findings in the order of the file, ties in the order they were met
func CtSortFound(xF)
	xOut = []
	for i = 1 to Len(xF)
		nAt = Len(xOut) + 1
		for j = Len(xOut) to 1 step -1
			if xOut[j][3] > xF[i][3]
				nAt = j
			else
				exit
			end
		end
		Insert(xOut, nAt - 1, xF[i])
	end
	return xOut
end
func CtSetCode(tCode, xCites)
	if tCode = "" tCode = "PARSE" end
	$tCourtCode = tCode
	if tCode = "PARSE"
		$xCourtCites = []
	else
		$xCourtCites = xCites
	end
end
# a declaration kind's CODES entry for a seat, or ""
func CtCodeFor(xKind, tSeat)
	if Len(xKind) < 6 return "" end
	for i = 1 to Len(xKind[6])
		if xKind[6][i][1] = tSeat return xKind[6][i][2] end
	end
	return ""
end
# the code and cites of a refusal that a declaration element owns: the
# element's CODE when it has one (cited as rule:<CODE>), else a default code
# cited as rule:<element name>
func CtElementCode(tOwn, tDefault, tName)
	if tOwn != "" return [tOwn, ["rule:" + tOwn]] end
	return [tDefault, ["rule:" + tName]]
end
# v0.28 (HARO-MENU-CITES-01): an element's code and cites, its declared CITES over the default -- the row's
# nth element, present only when declared: the string "none" cites nothing, a list cites what it names
func CtElementCites(tOwn, tDefault, tName, vRow, nN)
	xCC = CtElementCode(tOwn, tDefault, tName)
	if Len(vRow) < nN return xCC end
	if IsString(vRow[nN])
		xCC[2] = []
	elseif Len(vRow[nN]) > 0
		xCC[2] = vRow[nN]
	end
	return xCC
end
# v0.23: whether the court's own language is under an article of its CONSTITUTION
# (charter 2): the forged court carries ARTICLES in $aCourtConstitution, empty without one.
# A refusal that enforces an article names it -- "[Art. N name]" -- and cites "article:N",
# the number-and-article shape of COMPASS-KERN-06; a language under no constitution prints
# what it printed before, to the byte.
func CtUnderArticle(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($vCourtConstitution)
		if $vCourtConstitution[i] = tName return true end
	end
	return false
end
# v0.24: whether a seat is the zone's sovereign or movement seat (organizational_sovereignty, 5):
# the forged court carries [zone kind, sovereign seat, movement seat] in $aCourtZone, empty under none
func CtZoneSeat(tKindName, tSeat)
	if Len($vCourtZone) < 3 return false end
	if tKindName != $vCourtZone[1] return false end
	return (tSeat = $vCourtZone[2] or tSeat = $vCourtZone[3])
end
# v0.25: whether a point (kind.seat) is one of the constitution's PERSONAL seats
func CtIsPersonal(tPoint)
	for i = 1 to Len($vCourtPersonal)
		if $vCourtPersonal[i] = tPoint return true end
	end
	return false
end
# v0.25: the warnings a court collected (a CONSTRAINT of SEVERITY warning), as C2 diagnostics
func CtAppendWarnings(vDiags, tFile)
	for i = 1 to Len($vCourtWarnings)
		xW = $vCourtWarnings[i]
		vDiags + [xW[1], "warning", xW[4], tFile, xW[3], xW[2]]
	end
end
# v0.24: the audit chain of a sentence under visible_state (3): every refinement event, admitted
# or refused, is one JSON line appended beside the sentence (<file>.audit), numbered in order --
# no clock, so both runtimes write the same bytes; `audit <file>` answers the chain as a query.
# Nothing is written under no visible_state: the chain is the article's mechanism, not a side effect.
func CtAuditWrite(tVerdict, tStage, tCode)
	if $tCourtAuditFile = "" return end
	tOld = ""
	if FExists($tCourtAuditFile) tOld = Read($tCourtAuditFile) end
	nEv = 0
	for i = 1 to Len(tOld)
		if tOld[i] = Char(10) nEv++ end
	end
	xP = $vCourtAuditProposal
	# v0.25: a personal point's values enter the chain redacted (W4.4: a log carries no personal datum)
	tFromA = xP[3]
	tToA = xP[4]
	if Len(xP) >= 7
		if CtIsPersonal(xP[7])
			tFromA = "[personal]"
			tToA = "[personal]"
		end
	end
	tLine = '{"event": ' + String(nEv + 1) + ', "proposal": ' + CtJson(xP[1]) + ', "target": ' + CtJson(xP[2]) +
	        ', "from": ' + CtJson(tFromA) + ', "to": ' + CtJson(tToA) + ', "author": ' + CtJson(xP[5]) +
	        ', "posture": ' + CtJson(xP[6]) + ', "verdict": ' + CtJson(tVerdict) + ', "stage": ' + CtJson(tStage) +
	        ', "code": ' + CtJson(tCode) + '}'
	Write($tCourtAuditFile, tOld + tLine + Char(10))
end
# a REFUSAL category's code, codes per NAMED word and cites
func CtRefusalRow(tCategory)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtRefusals)
		if $xCourtRefusals[i][1] = tCategory return $xCourtRefusals[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtRefusalCode(tCategory, tWord, tDefault)
	xR = CtRefusalRow(tCategory)
	if IsEmpty(xR) return [tDefault, []] end
	tCode = ""
	if tWord != "" and Len(xR) >= 5
		for i = 1 to Len(xR[5])
			if xR[5][i][1] = tWord tCode = xR[5][i][2] end
		end
	end
	if tCode = "" and Len(xR) >= 4 tCode = xR[4] end
	if tCode = "" tCode = tDefault end
	xCites = []
	if Len(xR) >= 6
		if IsList(xR[6]) xCites = xR[6] end
	end
	return [tCode, xCites]
end
func CtInList(tS, xL)
	for i = 1 to Len(xL)
		if xL[i] = tS return true end
	end
	return false
end
func CtJoin(xL, tSep)
	tOut = ""
	for i = 1 to Len(xL)
		if i > 1 tOut += tSep end
		tOut += xL[i]
	end
	return tOut
end
# the declared refusal message of a category, or ""
# v0.8: a refusal's NAMED word -- its own message, or ""
func CtRefusalNamed(tCategory, tWord)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtRefusals)
		if $xCourtRefusals[i][1] = tCategory and Len($xCourtRefusals[i]) >= 3
			xN = $xCourtRefusals[i][3]
			for j = 1 to Len(xN)
				if xN[j][1] = tWord return xN[j][2] end
			end
		end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtRefusalMessage(tCategory)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtRefusals)
		if $xCourtRefusals[i][1] = tCategory return $xCourtRefusals[i][2] end
	end
	return ""
end
# ---- v0.4: one court, several languages ------------------------------------------
# The generated court carries $aCourtLangs, one record per language -- its own
# first, then every language a SENTENCE names, recursively: [name, ext, kinds,
# forms, refusals, menus, ranges, formats, unions, constraints, world, points,
# floors, views, sentences]. CtUseLanguage loads one record into the tables
# the court reads; a SENTENCE seat is judged by switching to its language and
# back, the judged declarations kept in $aCourtSentences for the conditions
# that read through them.

func CtDirOf(tPath)
	nN = 0
	for i = 1 to Len(tPath)
		if tPath[i] = "/" or tPath[i] = Char(92) nN = i end
	end
	if nN = 0 return "" end
	return Left(tPath, nN - 1)
end
func CtReplace(tS, tOld, tNew)
	tOut = ""
	nI = 1
	nN = Len(tS)
	nM = Len(tOld)
	while nI <= nN
		if nI + nM - 1 <= nN and SubStr(tS, nI, nM) = tOld
			tOut += tNew
			nI += nM
		else
			tOut += tS[nI]
			nI++
		end
	end
	return tOut
end
func CtLangEntry(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($vCourtLangs)
		if $vCourtLangs[i][1] = tName return $vCourtLangs[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtUseLanguage(tName)
	xE = CtLangEntry(tName)
	if IsEmpty(xE) Raise("the court carries no language called '" + tName + "'") end
	$tCourtLang = xE[1]
	$tCourtExt = xE[2]
	$xCourtKinds = xE[3]
	$xCourtForms = xE[4]
	$xCourtRefusals = xE[5]
	$xCourtMenus = xE[6]
	$xCourtRanges = xE[7]
	$xCourtFormats = xE[8]
	$xCourtUnions = xE[9]
	$xCourtConstraints = xE[10]
	$xCourtWorld = xE[11]
	$xCourtPoints = xE[12]
	$xCourtFloors = xE[13]
	$xCourtViews = xE[14]
	$xCourtSentenceKinds = xE[15]
	# v0.6: the EXPRESSIONs [name, ops, opds, aggs, vars, contexts, absent,
	# division, equality] and the WALKs [name, of, steps, through, order,
	# guards, compute, formula, fail]
	$xCourtExprs = []
	$xCourtWalks = []
	if Len(xE) >= 17
		$xCourtExprs = xE[16]
		$xCourtWalks = xE[17]
	end
	# v0.7: the ASK [name, from kinds, where, clauses], or NULL
	$xCourtAsk = ""
	if Len(xE) >= 18 $xCourtAsk = xE[18] end
	# v0.9: the RUN [[role, [kind, seat, ...]], ...], or NULL
	$xCourtRun = ""
	if Len(xE) >= 19 $xCourtRun = xE[19] end
	# v0.10: the SYMBOLs [name, kind, ref, message]
	$xCourtSymbols = []
	if Len(xE) >= 20 $xCourtSymbols = xE[20] end
	# v0.12: the FORMS [name, fluent, passive, statement, params, family], or NULL
	$xCourtFormset = ""
	if Len(xE) >= 21 $xCourtFormset = xE[21] end
	# v0.13: the NARRATE [name, opens, ends, refuses, says], or NULL
	$xCourtNarrate = ""
	if Len(xE) >= 22 $xCourtNarrate = xE[22] end
	# v0.17: the UNDERSTAND [name, [[role, kind], ...]], or NULL -- a human language reaches closed questions (n_lib.haro)
	$xCourtUnderstand = ""
	if Len(xE) >= 23 $xCourtUnderstand = xE[23] end
end
# the condition tables of every language the court carries, built once
func CtBuildCondLangs
	$xCondLangs = []
	for i = 1 to Len($vCourtLangs)
		xE = $vCourtLangs[i]
		xKinds = xE[3]
		xSents = xE[15]
		vDeclSeats = []
		vVerbOf = []
		for j = 1 to Len(xKinds)
			xS = xKinds[j][3]
			xInfo = []
			for k = 1 to Len(xS)
				tTK = "prim"
				if Len(xS[k]) >= 5 tTK = xS[k][5] end
				tTarget = ""
				if tTK = "decl" tTarget = xE[1] end
				if tTK = "sentence"
					for m = 1 to Len(xSents)
						if xSents[m][1] = xS[k][2] tTarget = xSents[m][2] end
					end
				end
				xInfo + [xS[k][1], xS[k][2], xS[k][3], tTK, tTarget]
			end
			vDeclSeats + [xKinds[j][2], xInfo]
			vVerbOf + [xKinds[j][2], xKinds[j][1]]
		end
		xViews = []
		for j = 1 to Len(xE[14])
			xV = xE[14][j]
			xViews + [xV[1], xV[2], "", xV[3], xV[4], xV[5]]
		end
		# v0.8: the WORLD's ENTRY kinds and the forms' seat kinds
		xEntry = []
		if Len(xE[11]) >= 3 xEntry = xE[11][3] end
		vFormTable = []
		for j = 1 to Len(xE[4])
			xFS = xE[4][j][2]
			xInfo = []
			for k = 1 to Len(xFS)
				xInfo + [xFS[k][1], xFS[k][2], CtTypeKind(xFS[k])]
			end
			vFormTable + [xE[4][j][1], xInfo]
		end
		$xCondLangs + [xE[1], vDeclSeats, xE[11][1], xViews, vVerbOf, xEntry, vFormTable]
	end
end
# the court's state, so a SENTENCE can be judged in its own language and the
# judge returned to its own; $aCourtSentences and $aCondLangs are shared
func CtSnapshot
	return [$tCourtLang, $tCourtExt, $tCourtDir, $xCourtKinds, $xCourtForms, $xCourtRefusals,
	        $xCourtMenus, $xCourtRanges, $xCourtFormats, $xCourtUnions, $xCourtConstraints,
	        $xCourtWorld, $xCourtPoints, $xCourtFloors, $xCourtViews, $xCourtSentenceKinds,
	        $xCourtToks, $nCourtPos, $xCondDecls, $tCondLang, $tCondOther, $bCondUnread,
	        $xCondFormats, $xCondToks, $nCondPos, $xCourtExprs, $xCourtWalks, $xCourtAsk, $xCourtRun,
	        $xCourtSymbols, $xCourtWorldFile, $xCourtFormset, $xCourtNarrate, $xCourtUnderstand]
end
func CtRestore(xS)
	$tCourtLang = xS[1]
	$tCourtExt = xS[2]
	$tCourtDir = xS[3]
	$xCourtKinds = xS[4]
	$xCourtForms = xS[5]
	$xCourtRefusals = xS[6]
	$xCourtMenus = xS[7]
	$xCourtRanges = xS[8]
	$xCourtFormats = xS[9]
	$xCourtUnions = xS[10]
	$xCourtConstraints = xS[11]
	$xCourtWorld = xS[12]
	$xCourtPoints = xS[13]
	$xCourtFloors = xS[14]
	$xCourtViews = xS[15]
	$xCourtSentenceKinds = xS[16]
	$xCourtToks = xS[17]
	$nCourtPos = xS[18]
	$xCondDecls = xS[19]
	$tCondLang = xS[20]
	$tCondOther = xS[21]
	$bCondUnread = xS[22]
	$xCondFormats = xS[23]
	$xCondToks = xS[24]
	$nCondPos = xS[25]
	$xCourtExprs = xS[26]
	$xCourtWalks = xS[27]
	$xCourtAsk = xS[28]
	$xCourtRun = xS[29]
	$xCourtSymbols = xS[30]
	$xCourtWorldFile = xS[31]
	$xCourtFormset = xS[32]
	$xCourtNarrate = xS[33]
	$xCourtUnderstand = xS[34]
end
# ---- v0.11: the Diagnostic Contract (C2 v1.2.0) -------------------------------------
# `diagnose <file> [world]` runs the same court and answers in the family's
# machine form: one object carrying `diagnostics`, each a six-field envelope --
# code, severity, message, span {file, line}, cites, language. A refusal is one
# error (the court stops at the first); a sentence with SYMBOL seats and no
# world adds one NO_WORLD warning at line 0; a clean run is `"diagnostics": []`.
# No value is ever a bare true, false or null (C2 2.8).

func CtStripPrefix(tMsg)
	nN = SubStr(tMsg, "): ")
	if nN > 0 return SubStr(tMsg, nN + 3) end
	return tMsg
end
func CtLineOf(tMsg)
	nAt = SubStr(tMsg, "(line ")
	if nAt = 0 return 0 end
	nEnd = SubStr(tMsg, "): ")
	if nEnd <= nAt return 0 end
	return Number(SubStr(tMsg, nAt + 6, nEnd - nAt - 6))
end
func CtDiagnosticJson(xD)
	tC = '{"code": ' + CtJson(xD[1]) + ', "severity": ' + CtJson(xD[2]) + ', "message": ' + CtJson(xD[3])
	tC += ', "span": {"file": ' + CtJson(xD[4]) + ', "line": ' + String(xD[5]) + '}, "cites": ['
	for i = 1 to Len(xD[6])
		if i > 1 tC += ", " end
		tC += CtJson(xD[6][i])
	end
	tC += '], "language": ' + CtJson($tCourtLang) + '}'
	return tC
end
func CtDiagnosticsJson(vDiags)
	tC = '{"diagnostics": ['
	for i = 1 to Len(vDiags)
		if i > 1 tC += ", " end
		tC += CtDiagnosticJson(vDiags[i])
	end
	return tC + ']}'
end
func CtDiagnose(tFile, tWorldPath)
	vDiags = []
	tSrc = Read(tFile)
	CtSetCode("PARSE", [])
	$vCourtWarnings = []
	# v0.14: this verb collects -- every pass goes on past a refusal to its next element
	$bCourtCollect = true
	$vCourtFound = []
	$vCourtBroken = []
	tErr = ""
	xDecls = ""
	try
		if tWorldPath != "" $xCourtWorldFile = CtWorldLoad(tWorldPath) end
		xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
	catch
		tErr = cCatchError
	end
	$bCourtCollect = false
	# a refusal nothing could resume from (the sentence did not parse, or a pass met
	# something it cannot judge past) ends the run and is the last finding
	if tErr != ""
		$vCourtFound + [$tCourtCode, $xCourtCites, CtLineOf(tErr), CtStripPrefix(tErr)]
	end
	if Len($vCourtFound) > 0
		xF = CtSortFound($vCourtFound)
		for i = 1 to Len(xF)
			vDiags + [xF[i][1], "error", xF[i][4], tFile, xF[i][3], xF[i][2]]
		end
		CtAppendWarnings(vDiags, tFile)
		return vDiags
	end
	CtAppendWarnings(vDiags, tFile)
	if IsEmpty($xCourtWorldFile) and Len($xCourtSymbols) > 0
		xSites = CtSymbolSites(xDecls)
		if Len(xSites) > 0
			xSy = CtSymbolByName(xSites[1][2][2])
			xCites = []
			if not IsEmpty(xSy) xCites = CtSymbolCode(xSy)[2] end
			vDiags + ["NO_WORLD", "warning", "no world to resolve against; " + String(Len(xSites)) + " symbol reference(s) unresolved, which is what C3 section 3.2 asks a project to close", tFile, 0, xCites]
		end
	end
	return vDiags
end
# ---- v0.6: the EXPRESSION tables, handed to expr_lib.haro ----------------------

func CtExprByName(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtExprs)
		if $xCourtExprs[i][1] = tName return $xCourtExprs[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtExprUse(xE)
	$tExprLang = xE[1]
	$xExprOperators = xE[2]
	$xExprOperands = xE[3]
	$xExprAggregates = xE[4]
	$xExprVariables = xE[5]
	$xExprContexts = xE[6]
	$tExprAbsent = xE[7]
	$tExprDivision = xE[8]
	$tExprEquality = xE[9]
end
# a SENTENCE seat type's record: [name, lang, message, refused]
func CtSentenceKind(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtSentenceKinds)
		if $xCourtSentenceKinds[i][1] = tName return $xCourtSentenceKinds[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
# a kind's MESSAGES entry for a seat, or ""
func CtMessageFor(xKind, tSeat)
	if Len(xKind) < 5 return "" end
	for i = 1 to Len(xKind[5])
		if xKind[5][i][1] = tSeat return xKind[5][i][2] end
	end
	return ""
end
# judge the file a SENTENCE seat names, beside the file being judged, with
# the language's own tables; keep its declarations, or refuse in the
# sentence's own words
func CtJudgeSentence(xDecl, xSeat, xClause)
	tRel = xClause[3][2]
	xSK = CtSentenceKind(xSeat[2])
	if IsEmpty(xSK) CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + xClause[1] + " names a SENTENCE the court does not carry") end
	tPath = tRel
	if $tCourtDir != "" tPath = $tCourtDir + "/" + tRel end
	if tRel = "" or not FExists(tPath)
		tMsg = xSK[3]
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = "{VERB} {name} names {value}, which cannot be read from beside this file" end
		CtFail(xClause[2], CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tRel))
	end
	tText = Read(tPath)
	xSnap = CtSnapshot()
	CtUseLanguage(xSK[2])
	$tCourtDir = CtDirOf(tPath)
	tErr = ""
	xInner = ""
	bWas = $bCourtCollect
	$bCourtCollect = false
	try
		xInner = CtDeclare(tText)
	catch
		tErr = cCatchError
	end
	$bCourtCollect = bWas
	CtRestore(xSnap)
	if tErr != ""
		# "<lang> (line N): why" -> why and N
		tWhy = tErr
		tLine = "?"
		nAt = SubStr(tErr, "(line ")
		if nAt > 0
			nEnd = SubStr(tErr, "): ")
			if nEnd > nAt
				tLine = SubStr(tErr, nAt + 6, nEnd - nAt - 6)
				tWhy = SubStr(tErr, nEnd + 3)
			end
		end
		tMsg = xSK[4]
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = "{VERB} {name} is refused: {why} (line {line} of {value})" end
		tMsg = CtReplace(CtReplace(tMsg, "{why}", tWhy), "{line}", tLine)
		CtFailC(xDecl[3], "SENTENCE", [], CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tRel))
	end
	$vCourtSentences + [$tCourtLang, xDecl[1], xDecl[2], xSeat[1], tRel, xInner, xSK[2]]
end
# ---- tokenizer: the Commons' lexical form, as harb's court reads it ---------
# a token is [type, text, line]; types: string number ident keyword
# lparen rparen lbracket rbracket comma eof

func CtTokenize(tSrc)
	# v0.30: the one lexer (block_lib.haro) reads the sentence; the court keeps its own words for what it refuses,
	# in the language's voice (unexpected_character). A `?` and a `.` are C6 (Q-B1, paths) and read by the lexer;
	# a sentence has no use for either, so the court refuses them as it always did. A comment is layout to a court
	xToks = BlkTokenize(tSrc)
	xOut = []
	for i = 1 to Len(xToks)
		xT = xToks[i]
		if xT[1] = "comment" loop end
		if xT[1] = "question" or xT[1] = "dot"
			CtFailChar(xT[3], xT[2])
		end
		if xT[1] = "error"
			if xT[2] = "unterminated_string"
				CtFail(xT[3], "Unterminated string")
			elseif xT[2] = "mixed_case"
				CtFail(xT[3], "'" + xT[4] + "' is neither a lower_snake identifier nor an UPPER_SNAKE keyword")
			elseif xT[2] = "number_glued"
				CtFail(xT[3], "'" + xT[4] + "' is neither a number nor a word")
			elseif xT[2] = "doubled_quote"
				CtFail(xT[3], "a doubled quote inside a string waits for C6's amendment (Q-B2): Ringua writes it; today a C6 string has no escape")
			else
				CtFailChar(xT[3], xT[4])
			end
		end
		xOut + xT
	end
	return xOut
end
func CtFailChar(nLine, tC)
	tMsgC = CtRefusalMessage("unexpected_character")
	if tMsgC != "" tMsgC = " -- " + tMsgC end
	CtFail(nLine, "The character '" + tC + "' is not part of the " + $tCourtLang + " grammar" + tMsgC)
end
# ---- the tables, read ---------------------------------------------------------

func CtKindByVerb(tVerb)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtKinds)
		if $xCourtKinds[i][1] = tVerb return $xCourtKinds[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtVerbs
	xV = []
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtKinds)
		xV + $xCourtKinds[i][1]
	end
	return xV
end
func CtFormByName(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtForms)
		if $xCourtForms[i][1] = tName return $xCourtForms[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
# a seat is [name, of, isList, optional, typeKind]; its clause name is the
# seat's name in UPPER_SNAKE, and its value shape follows its type:
#   text / a FORMAT -> string, name/flag/ref / a MENU / a DECLARATION -> word,
#   number / a RANGE -> number, [form] -> a list whose items follow the form's
#   first seat (text or a FORMAT -> stringlist, else namelist), [decl] and
#   [menu] -> namelist
func CtTypeKind(xSeat)
	if Len(xSeat) >= 5 return xSeat[5] end
	return "prim"
end
func CtIsPairForm(xFS)
	# v0.27: a third, optional MENU seat is the mark, written after the value
	if Len(xFS) != 2 and not CtHasMarkSeat(xFS) return false end
	if xFS[1][3] or xFS[2][3] return false end
	tK1 = CtTypeKind(xFS[1])
	if xFS[1][2] != "name" and tK1 != "menu" and tK1 != "decl" return false end
	return true
end
# v0.27: the mark seat of a pair form -- third, optional, a MENU
func CtHasMarkSeat(xFS)
	if Len(xFS) != 3 return false end
	if xFS[3][3] or not xFS[3][4] return false end
	return CtTypeKind(xFS[3]) = "menu"
end
# v0.8: does a seat take part in the references pass -- a reference, a UNION
# of declarations, or a pair list whose keys or values are references -- and
# in the local pass -- everything else, and a pair list's menu keys and
# scalar values
func CtUnionHasDecls(tName)
	xU = CtUnionByName(tName)
	if IsEmpty(xU) return false end
	for i = 1 to Len(xU[2])
		if xU[2][i][3] = "decl" return true end
	end
	return false
end
func CtSeatPasses(xSeat)
	tK = CtTypeKind(xSeat)
	if tK = "decl" return [false, true] end
	if xSeat[3] and tK = "union" return [false, true] end
	if tK = "union"
		if CtUnionHasDecls(xSeat[2]) return [true, true] end
		return [true, false]
	end
	if xSeat[3] and tK = "form"
		xF = CtFormByName(xSeat[2])
		if not IsEmpty(xF) and CtIsPairForm(xF[2])
			bRef = false
			if CtTypeKind(xF[2][1]) = "decl" bRef = true end
			if CtTypeKind(xF[2][2]) = "decl" bRef = true end
			if CtTypeKind(xF[2][2]) = "union" and CtUnionHasDecls(xF[2][2][2]) bRef = true end
			return [true, bRef]
		end
	end
	return [true, false]
end
func CtClauseShape(xSeat)
	tOf = xSeat[2]
	tK = CtTypeKind(xSeat)
	if xSeat[3]
		if tK = "union" return "namelist" end
		if tK = "form"
			xF = CtFormByName(tOf)
			if IsEmpty(xF) return "namelist" end
			xFS = xF[2]
			# v0.6: a FORM that is a name and a scalar is written as pairs
			if CtIsPairForm(xFS) return "pairlist" end
			if Len(xFS) > 0 and (xFS[1][2] = "text" or CtTypeKind(xFS[1]) = "format") return "stringlist" end
		end
		return "namelist"
	end
	if tK = "union" return "union" end
	if tK = "sentence" return "string" end
	if tK = "expr" return "string" end
	if tK = "symbol" return "word" end
	if tOf = "text" or tK = "format" return "string" end
	if tOf = "number" or tK = "range" return "number" end
	return "word"
end
func CtMenuByName(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtMenus)
		if $xCourtMenus[i][1] = tName return $xCourtMenus[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtRangeByName(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtRanges)
		if $xCourtRanges[i][1] = tName return $xCourtRanges[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtFormatByName(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtFormats)
		if $xCourtFormats[i][1] = tName return $xCourtFormats[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtKindByDeclName(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtKinds)
		if $xCourtKinds[i][2] = tName return $xCourtKinds[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
# ---- v0.3: a UNION seat takes a value of one of several shapes -------------------
# a union is [name, [[of, isList, typeKind], ...], message]

func CtUnionByName(tName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtUnions)
		if $xCourtUnions[i][1] = tName return $xCourtUnions[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
# an alternative's value shape, as CtClauseShape gives a seat's
func CtAltShape(xAlt)
	return CtClauseShape([xAlt[1], xAlt[1], xAlt[2], 0, xAlt[3]])
end
# the alternative whose shape the written value has, or NULL; an empty list
# fits either list shape
func CtUnionAlt(xSeat, xClause)
	xU = CtUnionByName(xSeat[2])
	if IsEmpty(xU) return "" end
	tGot = xClause[3][1]
	bEmpty = false
	if tGot = "namelist" or tGot = "stringlist"
		if Len(xClause[3][2]) = 0 bEmpty = true end
	end
	xAlts = xU[2]
	for i = 1 to Len(xAlts)
		tShape = CtAltShape(xAlts[i])
		if tShape = tGot return xAlts[i] end
		if bEmpty and (tShape = "namelist" or tShape = "stringlist") return xAlts[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
# the union's own MESSAGE speaks when the value fits no alternative
func CtWantUnion(xDecl, xClause, xSeat)
	if not IsEmpty(CtUnionAlt(xSeat, xClause)) return end
	xU = CtUnionByName(xSeat[2])
	if IsEmpty(xU) CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + xClause[1] + " names a UNION the court does not carry") end
	tMsg = xU[3]
	if tMsg = ""
		xNames = []
		for i = 1 to Len(xU[2])
			xNames + xU[2][i][1]
		end
		tMsg = "Clause " + xClause[1] + " takes one of " + CtJoin(xNames, ", ")
	end
	tV = ""
	if xClause[3][1] = "word" or xClause[3][1] = "string" or xClause[3][1] = "number" tV = xClause[3][2] end
	tOwn = ""
	if Len(xU) >= 4 tOwn = xU[4] end
	xCC = CtElementCites(tOwn, "UNION", xU[1], xU, 5)
	CtFailC(xClause[2], xCC[1], xCC[2], CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tV))
end
# {name}, {VERB}, {value}, {other}, {seat} and {decl.seat} in a declared message
func CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tValue)
	tOut = ""
	nN = Len(tMsg)
	nI = 1
	while nI <= nN
		tC = tMsg[nI]
		if tC = "{"
			nJ = nI + 1
			while nJ <= nN and tMsg[nJ] != "}"
				nJ++
			end
			if nJ > nN
				tOut += tC
				nI++
				loop
			end
			tKey = SubStr(tMsg, nI + 1, nJ - nI - 1)
			tRep = ""
			if tKey = "name"
				if not IsEmpty(xDecl) tRep = xDecl[2] end
			elseif tKey = "VERB"
				if not IsEmpty(xDecl) tRep = xDecl[1] end
			elseif tKey = "value"
				tRep = tValue
			elseif tKey = "other"
				tRep = $tCondOther
			else
				if not IsEmpty(xDecl)
					xV = CondScalar(xDecl, tKey)
					if not IsEmpty(xV)
						tRep = xV
					else
						xL = CondListOf(xDecl, tKey)
						if not IsEmpty(xL)
							tRep = CtJoin(xL, ", ")
						else
							# a path: {x.seat} through a reference seat, a ONE kind or a
							# VIEW, {view} a VIEW's declaration (v0.3, v0.4)
							bSave = $bCondUnread
							xV = CondPathScalar(["path", CondSplit(tKey, ".")], ["decl", $tCondLang, xDecl, $xCondDecls], "")
							$bCondUnread = bSave
							if not IsEmpty(xV) tRep = xV end
						end
					end
				end
			end
			tOut += tRep
			nI = nJ + 1
		else
			tOut += tC
			nI++
		end
	end
	return tOut
end
# ---- the shapes of a FORMAT -----------------------------------------------------

func CtIsHexChar(tC)
	nN = Ascii(tC)
	return (nN >= 48 and nN <= 57) or (nN >= 97 and nN <= 102) or (nN >= 65 and nN <= 70)
end
func CtIsLabelChar(tC)
	nN = Ascii(tC)
	return (nN >= 97 and nN <= 122) or (nN >= 48 and nN <= 57) or nN = 45
end
func CtIsIpv4(tS)
	xParts = CtSplit(tS, ".")
	if Len(xParts) != 4 return false end
	for i = 1 to 4
		xP = xParts[i]
		if Len(xP) = 0 or Len(xP) > 3 return false end
		for j = 1 to Len(xP)
			if not CtIsDigit(xP[j]) return false end
		end
		if Number(xP) > 255 return false end
	end
	return true
end
func CtSplit(tS, tSep)
	xOut = []
	tCur = ""
	for i = 1 to Len(tS)
		if tS[i] = tSep
			xOut + tCur
			tCur = ""
		else
			tCur += tS[i]
		end
	end
	xOut + tCur
	return xOut
end
func CtIsLabel(tS)
	if Len(tS) = 0 return false end
	for i = 1 to Len(tS)
		if not CtIsLabelChar(tS[i]) return false end
	end
	if tS[1] = "-" or tS[Len(tS)] = "-" return false end
	return true
end
# one definition of the shapes, in cond_lib.haro, since v0.3's `matches`
# tests them inside a condition too
func CtHasShape(tS, tShape)
	return CondHasShape(tS, tShape)
end
func CtAllowedClauses(xKind)
	xS = xKind[3]
	xOut = []
	for i = 1 to Len(xS)
		xOut + Upper(xS[i][1])
	end
	return xOut
end
func CtSeatByClause(xKind, tClause)
	xS = xKind[3]
	for i = 1 to Len(xS)
		if Upper(xS[i][1]) = tClause return xS[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
# ---- parser ----------------------------------------------------------------

func CtPeek
	return $xCourtToks[$nCourtPos]
end
func CtNext
	xT = $xCourtToks[$nCourtPos]
	if xT[1] != "eof" $nCourtPos++ end
	return xT
end
func CtShown(xT)
	if xT[1] = "eof" return "end of file" end
	return xT[2]
end
func CtExpect(tType, tWhat)
	xT = CtNext()
	if xT[1] != tType
		CtFail(xT[3], "Expected " + tWhat + ", found '" + CtShown(xT) + "'")
	end
	return xT
end
# a value is [shape, payload, start, end]: word/string/number carry text;
# namelist and stringlist carry a list; an empty list is [namelist, []];
# start and end are the value's byte span in the source
func CtParseValue
	xT = CtNext()
	if xT[1] = "ident" return ["word", xT[2], xT[4], xT[5]] end
	if xT[1] = "string" return ["string", xT[2], xT[4], xT[5]] end
	if xT[1] = "number" return ["number", xT[2], xT[4], xT[5]] end
	if xT[1] = "lbracket"
		xNames = []
		vStrings = []
		vPairs = []
		while true
			xE = CtPeek()
			if xE[1] = "rbracket"
				CtNext()
				exit
			end
			xItem = CtNext()
			if xItem[1] = "ident" and CtPeek()[1] = "colon"
				# v0.6: a name: value pair; the value a word, a string or a number
				CtNext()
				xTv = CtNext()
				if xTv[1] != "ident" and xTv[1] != "string" and xTv[1] != "number"
					CtFail(xTv[3], "A pair's value is a word, a string or a number, found '" + CtShown(xTv) + "'")
				end
				vPair = [xItem[2], xTv[2], xTv[1], ""]
				# v0.27: a mark after the value -- `member: text personal`
				if CtPeek()[1] = "ident"
					xTm = CtNext()
					vPair[4] = xTm[2]
				end
				vPairs + vPair
			elseif xItem[1] = "ident"
				xNames + xItem[2]
			elseif xItem[1] = "string"
				vStrings + xItem[2]
			else
				CtFail(xItem[3], "A list holds words or strings, found '" + CtShown(xItem) + "'")
			end
			xSep = CtPeek()
			if xSep[1] = "comma"
				CtNext()
			elseif xSep[1] != "rbracket"
				CtFail(xSep[3], "Expected ',' or ']' in a list, found '" + CtShown(xSep) + "'")
			end
		end
		if Len(xNames) > 0 and Len(vStrings) > 0
			CtFail(xT[3], "A list is all words or all strings, never mixed")
		end
		if Len(vPairs) > 0 and (Len(xNames) > 0 or Len(vStrings) > 0)
			CtFail(xT[3], "A list is all name: value pairs or none")
		end
		nListEnd = $xCourtToks[$nCourtPos - 1][5]
		if Len(vPairs) > 0 return ["pairlist", vPairs, xT[4], nListEnd] end
		if Len(vStrings) > 0 return ["stringlist", vStrings, xT[4], nListEnd] end
		return ["namelist", xNames, xT[4], nListEnd]
	end
	CtFail(xT[3], "Expected a clause value, found '" + CtShown(xT) + "'")
end
# one DEFINE <VERB> <name> AS ( clauses ) RATIONALE "..."
# returns [verb, name, line, clauses, rationale]; a clause is [NAME, line, value]
func CtParseDecl
	xV = CtNext()
	if not (xV[1] = "keyword" and xV[2] = "DEFINE")
		tMsg = CtRefusalMessage("unknown_verb")
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = "the " + $tCourtLang + " verb set is closed (DEFINE)" end
		xCC = CtRefusalCode("unknown_verb", "", "UNKNOWN_VERB")
		CtFailC(xV[3], xCC[1], xCC[2], "Unknown verb '" + CtShown(xV) + "': " + tMsg)
	end
	xK = CtNext()
	xKind = ""
	if xK[1] = "keyword" xKind = CtKindByVerb(xK[2]) end
	if IsEmpty(xKind)
		# v0.35: a NAMED kind held at warning is read past and said (severity_lib.haro, loaded only where one is held)
		xSevR = CtRefusalRow("unknown_declaration")
		if not IsEmpty(xSevR)
			if Len(xSevR) >= 7
				if SevSkipNamed(xSevR, xK) return "" end
			end
		end
		tNamed = CtRefusalNamed("unknown_declaration", Lower(CtShown(xK)))
		if tNamed != ""
			xCC = CtRefusalCode("unknown_declaration", Lower(CtShown(xK)), "UNKNOWN_KIND")
			CtFailC(xK[3], xCC[1], xCC[2], tNamed)
		end
		tMsg = CtRefusalMessage("unknown_declaration")
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = "the kinds are closed (" + CtJoin(CtVerbs(), ", ") + ")" end
		xCC = CtRefusalCode("unknown_declaration", "", "UNKNOWN_KIND")
		CtFailC(xK[3], xCC[1], [], "Unknown kind '" + CtShown(xK) + "': " + tMsg)
	end
	xName = CtExpect("ident", "a lower_snake name")
	xAs = CtNext()
	if not (xAs[1] = "keyword" and xAs[2] = "AS")
		CtFail(xAs[3], "Expected AS after the name, found '" + CtShown(xAs) + "'")
	end
	CtExpect("lparen", "'('")
	xClauses = []
	xAllowed = CtAllowedClauses(xKind)
	while true
		xT = CtPeek()
		if xT[1] = "rparen"
			CtNext()
			exit
		end
		xC = CtNext()
		if xC[1] != "keyword"
			CtFail(xC[3], "Expected a clause name, found '" + CtShown(xC) + "'")
		end
		if not CtInList(xC[2], xAllowed)
			tNamed = CtRefusalNamed("unknown_seat", Lower(xC[2]))
			if tNamed != ""
				xCC = CtRefusalCode("unknown_seat", Lower(xC[2]), "UNKNOWN_CLAUSE")
				CtFailC(xC[3], xCC[1], xCC[2], tNamed)
			end
			tMsg = CtRefusalMessage("unknown_seat")
			if tMsg = "" tMsg = "allowed are " + CtJoin(xAllowed, ", ") end
			xCC = CtRefusalCode("unknown_seat", "", "UNKNOWN_CLAUSE")
			CtFailC(xC[3], xCC[1], [], "Unknown clause '" + xC[2] + "' for " + xKind[1] + ": " + tMsg)
		end
		for i = 1 to Len(xClauses)
			if xClauses[i][1] = xC[2]
				CtFail(xC[3], "Clause " + xC[2] + " given twice")
			end
		end
		xVal = CtParseValue()
		# a FORMAT that FOLDs case reads its value folded (v0.4): hex is case-blind
		xSeatF = CtSeatByClause(xKind, xC[2])
		if not IsEmpty(xSeatF)
			if CtTypeKind(xSeatF) = "format" and xVal[1] = "string"
				xF = CtFormatByName(xSeatF[2])
				if not IsEmpty(xF)
					if Len(xF) >= 4
						if xF[4] = "case" xVal[2] = Lower(xVal[2]) end
					end
				end
			end
		end
		# a clause is [NAME, line, value, start, end] -- the value's span
		xClauses + [xC[2], xC[3], xVal, xVal[3], xVal[4]]
		xSep = CtPeek()
		if xSep[1] = "comma"
			CtNext()
		elseif xSep[1] != "rparen"
			CtFail(xSep[3], "Expected ',' or ')' after a clause, found '" + CtShown(xSep) + "'")
		end
	end
	xR = CtNext()
	if not (xR[1] = "keyword" and xR[2] = "RATIONALE")
		tMsgR = "RATIONALE is mandatory on every declaration (" + xKind[1] + " " + xName[2] + " has none)"
		# v0.23: under explainability the refusal is traceable (code RATIONALE) and names its article
		if CtUnderArticle("explainability")
			CtFailC(xR[3], "RATIONALE", ["article:1"], tMsgR + " [Art. 1 explainability]")
		end
		CtFail(xR[3], tMsgR)
	end
	xRS = CtExpect("string", "the RATIONALE string")
	return [xKind[1], xName[2], xName[3], xClauses, xRS[2]]
end
# ---- the structural court ---------------------------------------------------

func CtWantShape(xDecl, xClause, tShape)
	tGot = xClause[3][1]
	tName = xClause[1]
	if tShape = "word"
		if tGot != "word" CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + tName + " takes a word") end
	elseif tShape = "string"
		if tGot != "string" CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + tName + " takes a string") end
	elseif tShape = "number"
		if tGot != "number" CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + tName + " takes a number") end
	elseif tShape = "namelist"
		if tGot = "stringlist" and Len(xClause[3][2]) = 0 return end
		if tGot != "namelist" CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + tName + " takes a list of words") end
	elseif tShape = "stringlist"
		if tGot = "namelist" and Len(xClause[3][2]) = 0 return end
		if tGot != "stringlist" CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + tName + " takes a string list, one word per string") end
	elseif tShape = "pairlist"
		if tGot = "namelist" and Len(xClause[3][2]) = 0 return end
		if tGot != "pairlist" CtFail(xClause[2], "Clause " + tName + " takes name: value pairs") end
	end
end
# parse a whole source and judge what the declaration can judge; returns the
# list of declarations
func CtDeclare(tSrc)
	CtSetCode("PARSE", [])
	$xCourtToks = CtTokenize(tSrc)
	$nCourtPos = 1
	xDecls = []
	while CtPeek()[1] != "eof"
		# v0.35: a NAMED kind held at warning is read past, and declares nothing
		xPD = CtParseDecl()
		if not IsEmpty(xPD) xDecls + xPD end
	end
	if Len(xDecls) = 0
		CtFail(1, "A " + $tCourtLang + " file declares nothing")
	end
	# one namespace
	for i = 1 to Len(xDecls)
		for j = 1 to i - 1
			if xDecls[i][2] = xDecls[j][2]
				tMsg = CtRefusalMessage("duplicate_name")
				if tMsg = "" tMsg = "one namespace, no duplicates" end
				xCC = CtRefusalCode("duplicate_name", "", "DUPLICATE_NAME")
				try
					CtFailC(xDecls[i][3], xCC[1], xCC[2], "'" + String(xDecls[i][2]) + "' is already declared (line " + String(xDecls[j][3]) + "); " + tMsg)
				catch
					CtNote(cCatchError)
				end
				exit
			end
		end
	end
	# every clause's value has the seat's shape; every required seat is present
	for i = 1 to Len(xDecls)
		xD = xDecls[i]
		xKind = CtKindByVerb(xD[1])
		xC = xD[4]
		for j = 1 to Len(xC)
			xSeat = CtSeatByClause(xKind, xC[j][1])
			try
				if CtTypeKind(xSeat) = "union" and not xSeat[3]
					CtWantUnion(xD, xC[j], xSeat)
				else
					# a LIST of a union of declarations is a name list (v0.9)
					CtWantShape(xD, xC[j], CtClauseShape(xSeat))
				end
			catch
				CtNote(cCatchError)
				$vCourtBroken + i
			end
		end
		xSeats = xKind[3]
		for j = 1 to Len(xSeats)
			xSeat = xSeats[j]
			if xSeat[3] or xSeat[4] loop end
			bFound = false
			for k = 1 to Len(xC)
				if xC[k][1] = Upper(xSeat[1]) bFound = true end
			end
			if not bFound
				# the declaration's own MESSAGES for a required seat speaks first (v0.4);
				# its CODES give the envelope's code (v0.11)
				tMsgR = CtMessageFor(xKind, xSeat[1])
				tCodeR = CtCodeFor(xKind, xSeat[1])
				xCC = CtElementCode(tCodeR, "REQUIRED", xKind[2] + "." + xSeat[1])
				# v0.24: a zone without its holder or its entry is sovereignty's refusal (Art. 5)
				tArt5 = ""
				if CtUnderArticle("organizational_sovereignty")
					if CtZoneSeat(xKind[2], xSeat[1])
						xCites5 = xCC[2]
						xCites5 + "article:5"
						xCC[2] = xCites5
						tArt5 = " [Art. 5 organizational_sovereignty]"
					end
				end
				try
					if tMsgR != "" CtFailC(xD[3], xCC[1], xCC[2], CtFill(tMsgR, xD, "") + tArt5) end
					CtFailC(xD[3], xCC[1], xCC[2], Upper(xSeat[1]) + " is required on " + xD[1] + " " + xD[2] + tArt5)
				catch
					CtNote(cCatchError)
				end
			end
		end
	end

	# ---- v0.2: what the WORLD, the types, the names and the constraints say ----
	$xCondDecls = xDecls
	$tCondLang = $tCourtLang
	$xCondFormats = []
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtFormats)
		$xCondFormats + [$xCourtFormats[i][1], $xCourtFormats[i][2]]
	end

	# the WORLD: exactly one of each ONE kind, and the FIRST kind first
	xOne = $xCourtWorld[1]
	for i = 1 to Len(xOne)
		xK = CtKindByDeclName(xOne[i])
		if IsEmpty(xK) loop end
		nN = 0
		for j = 1 to Len(xDecls)
			if xDecls[j][1] = xK[1] nN++ end
		end
		if nN != 1
			try
				CtFailC(xDecls[1][3], "WORLD_ONE", ["rule:world"], "A " + $tCourtLang + " file declares exactly one " + String(xK[1]) + " (found " + String(nN) + ")")
			catch
				CtNote(cCatchError)
			end
		end
	end
	if $xCourtWorld[2] != ""
		xK = CtKindByDeclName($xCourtWorld[2])
		if not IsEmpty(xK) and xDecls[1][1] != xK[1]
			try
				CtFailC(xDecls[1][3], "WORLD_FIRST", ["rule:world"], "The " + xK[1] + " declaration comes first")
			catch
				CtNote(cCatchError)
			end
		end
	end

	# the NAMES of a declaration kind, and every seat's typed value -- the
	# local facts first (a menu, a range, a format, a union); a reference is a
	# fact about the whole sentence and is checked after the constraints, which
	# are the maker's own words about the whole sentence (v0.3)
	CtCheckValues(xDecls, false)

	# the CONSTRAINTs, each on every declaration of its ON kind; a condition
	# that reads through a reference that resolves to nothing says nothing,
	# and the reference's own refusal speaks below
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtConstraints)
		xCn = $xCourtConstraints[i]
		xK = CtKindByDeclName(xCn[2])
		if IsEmpty(xK) loop end
		xWhen = CondParse(xCn[3])
		xThen = ""
		if xCn[4] != "" xThen = CondParse(xCn[4]) end
		for j = 1 to Len(xDecls)
			xD = xDecls[j]
			if xD[1] != xK[1] loop end
			if CtIsBroken(j) loop end
			$tCondOther = ""
			$bCondUnread = false
			bWhen = CondEval(xWhen, xD)
			if $bCondUnread loop end
			if bWhen
				# WHEN alone names a forbidden state; with THEN, the consequence must hold
				bFail = true
				if not IsEmpty(xThen)
					bFail = not CondEval(xThen, xD)
					if $bCondUnread loop end
				end
				if bFail
					tCnC = ""
					if Len(xCn) >= 6 tCnC = xCn[6] end
					xCC = CtElementCode(tCnC, "CONSTRAINT", xCn[1])
					# v0.23: a CONSTRAINT that CITES cites what it declares, as a REFUSAL does. The
					# element is assigned, not the list rebuilt from its own element: on Ring 1.27
					# `a = [a[1], b]` reads a[1] from a list already emptied (R2), haro reads it
					# first -- HF-36, met again here (stage 29's L6 on the oracle, 2026-11-02)
					# v0.28: CITES none -- the row's "none" -- cites nothing
					if Len(xCn) >= 7
						if IsString(xCn[7])
							xCC[2] = []
						elseif Len(xCn[7]) > 0
							xCC[2] = xCn[7]
						end
					end
					# v0.25: a CONSTRAINT of SEVERITY warning is noted and spoken after the verdict, never raised
					tCnSev = "error"
					if Len(xCn) >= 8 tCnSev = xCn[8] end
					if tCnSev = "warning"
						$vCourtWarnings + [xCC[1], xCC[2], xD[3], CtFill(xCn[5], xD, "")]
					else
						try
							CtFailC(xD[3], xCC[1], xCC[2], CtFill(xCn[5], xD, ""))
						catch
							CtNote(cCatchError)
						end
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end

	# v0.32: the PATTERNs, each on the value of its OVER seat as the sentence writes it
	# (pattern_judge.haro, loaded by a court whose language declares a PATTERN: the language entry has a 24th element)
	xEPat = CtLangEntry($tCourtLang)
	if not IsEmpty(xEPat)
		# (v0.40: a language that NEEDS writes the 24th element empty when it declares no PATTERN)
		if Len(xEPat) >= 24
			if Len(xEPat[24]) > 0 CtCheckPatterns(xDecls, tSrc) end
		end
	end

	# the references, last
	CtCheckValues(xDecls, true)
	# v0.40: a door a sentence opens must be one its language NEEDS (needs_lib.haro, loaded where a language NEEDS: the entry has a 25th element)
	xENd = CtLangEntry($tCourtLang)
	if not IsEmpty(xENd)
		if Len(xENd) >= 25 NdCheck(xDecls, xENd[25]) end
	end
	# v0.9: an algorithm's step tree is a tree
	if not IsEmpty($xCourtRun)
		try
			RunCheckAcyclic(xDecls)
		catch
			CtNote(cCatchError)
		end
	end
	# v0.12: a family offers only forms the FORMS declares
	if not IsEmpty($xCourtFormset)
		try
			FormsCheck(xDecls)
		catch
			CtNote(cCatchError)
		end
	end
	# v0.17: the rules of a language that is UNDERSTOOD (n_lib.haro). They read a sentence whose references
	# resolve, so a sentence that already has a finding is not read by them; `check` stops at the first
	if not IsEmpty($xCourtUnderstand) and Len($vCourtFound) = 0
		try
			NatCheckRules(xDecls)
		catch
			CtNote(cCatchError)
		end
	end
	# v0.10: the symbols resolve against the world, when one is handed in
	if not IsEmpty($xCourtWorldFile) CtResolveWorld(xDecls) end
	return xDecls
end
# the NAMES and the typed seat values of every declaration: bRefs false checks
# the local types and skips the references, true the references alone
func CtCheckValues(xDecls, bRefs)
	for i = 1 to Len(xDecls)
		if CtIsBroken(i) loop end
		xD = xDecls[i]
		xKind = CtKindByVerb(xD[1])
		if not bRefs
			if Len(xKind) >= 4 and xKind[4] != ""
				tWhy = CtCheckNamed(xKind[4], xD[2])
				if tWhy != ""
					try
						CtFail(xD[3], "'" + xD[2] + "' " + tWhy)
					catch
						CtNote(cCatchError)
					end
				end
			end
		end
		xC = xD[4]
		for j = 1 to Len(xC)
			xSeat = CtSeatByClause(xKind, xC[j][1])
			xP = CtSeatPasses(xSeat)
			nPass = 1  if bRefs nPass = 2 end
			if not xP[nPass] loop end
			if CtTypeKind(xSeat) = "sentence"
				# v0.4: the file a SENTENCE seat names is judged in its own language
				try
					CtJudgeSentence(xD, xSeat, xC[j])
				catch
					CtNote(cCatchError)
				end
				loop
			end
			# v0.35: a reference seat held at warning speaks each element that resolves to nothing as a warning (severity_lib.haro)
			if bRefs and Len(xKind) >= 7
				if SevSeatIs(xKind, xSeat[1]) = "warning"
					SevWarnClause(xD, xSeat, xC[j])
					loop
				end
			end
			tWhy = CtCheckSeatValue(xD, xSeat, xC[j], bRefs)
			if tWhy != ""
				try
					CtFail(xC[j][2], tWhy)
				catch
					CtNote(cCatchError)
				end
			end
		end
	end
end
# a declaration's name against its kind's NAMES (a MENU or a FORMAT); "" or why
func CtCheckNamed(tNames, tName)
	xM = CtMenuByName(tNames)
	if not IsEmpty(xM)
		if CtInList(tName, xM[2]) return "" end
		tMsg = xM[3]
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = "is not a " + tNames + ": the menu is " + CtJoin(xM[2], ", ") end
		tOwn = ""
		if Len(xM) >= 4 tOwn = xM[4] end
		xCC = CtElementCites(tOwn, "MENU", xM[1], xM, 5)
		CtSetCode(xCC[1], xCC[2])
		return CtFill(tMsg, "", tName)
	end
	xF = CtFormatByName(tNames)
	if not IsEmpty(xF)
		if CtHasShape(tName, xF[2]) return "" end
		tMsg = xF[3]
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = "is not a " + xF[2] end
		tOwn = ""
		if Len(xF) >= 5 tOwn = xF[5] end
		xCC = CtElementCites(tOwn, "FORMAT", xF[1], xF, 6)
		CtSetCode(xCC[1], xCC[2])
		return CtFill(tMsg, "", tName)
	end
	return ""
end
# one scalar value against a seat's type (menu, range, format, reference); "" or why
func CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xSeat, tValue)
	tK = CtTypeKind(xSeat)
	tClause = Upper(xSeat[1])
	if tK = "menu"
		xM = CtMenuByName(xSeat[2])
		if IsEmpty(xM) or CtInList(tValue, xM[2]) return "" end
		tMsg = xM[3]
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = tClause + " is " + CtJoin(xM[2], ", ") end
		if SubStr(tMsg, "{value}") = 0 tMsg += ", not '{value}'" end
		tOwn = ""
		if Len(xM) >= 4 tOwn = xM[4] end
		xCC = CtElementCites(tOwn, "MENU", xM[1], xM, 5)
		CtSetCode(xCC[1], xCC[2])
		return CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tValue)
	elseif tK = "range"
		xR = CtRangeByName(xSeat[2])
		if IsEmpty(xR) return "" end
		nN = Number(tValue)
		if nN >= Number(xR[2]) and nN <= Number(xR[3]) return "" end
		tMsg = xR[4]
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = tClause + " {value} is out of range (" + xR[2] + ".." + xR[3] + ")" end
		tOwn = ""
		if Len(xR) >= 5 tOwn = xR[5] end
		xCC = CtElementCites(tOwn, "RANGE", xR[1], xR, 6)
		CtSetCode(xCC[1], xCC[2])
		return CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tValue)
	elseif tK = "format"
		xF = CtFormatByName(xSeat[2])
		if IsEmpty(xF) or CtHasShape(tValue, xF[2]) return "" end
		tMsg = xF[3]
		if tMsg = "" tMsg = tClause + " is not a " + xF[2] + ": '{value}'" end
		tOwn = ""
		if Len(xF) >= 5 tOwn = xF[5] end
		xCC = CtElementCites(tOwn, "FORMAT", xF[1], xF, 6)
		CtSetCode(xCC[1], xCC[2])
		return CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tValue)
	elseif tK = "expr"
		# v0.6: the text is an expression of the seat's language, or the refusal says why
		xE = CtExprByName(xSeat[2])
		if IsEmpty(xE) return "" end
		CtExprUse(xE)
		tErr = ""
		try
			ExParse(tValue, [])
		catch
			tErr = cCatchError
		end
		if tErr != ""
			CtSetCode("EXPRESSION", ["rule:" + xSeat[2]])
			return tClause + " of " + xDecl[1] + " " + xDecl[2] + " is not a " + xSeat[2] + " expression -- " + tErr
		end
		return ""
	elseif tK = "decl"
		xK = CtKindByDeclName(xSeat[2])
		if IsEmpty(xK) return "" end
		for i = 1 to Len($xCondDecls)
			if $xCondDecls[i][1] = xK[1] and $xCondDecls[i][2] = tValue return "" end
		end
		# the declaration's own MESSAGES for this seat speaks first (v0.3); its
		# CODES give the envelope's code (v0.11)
		xKd = CtKindByVerb(xDecl[1])
		xCC = CtElementCode(CtCodeFor(xKd, xSeat[1]), "DANGLING", xKd[2] + "." + xSeat[1])
		# v0.24: a zone entered through nothing is sovereignty's refusal (Art. 5)
		tArt5 = ""
		if CtUnderArticle("organizational_sovereignty")
			if CtZoneSeat(xKd[2], xSeat[1])
				xCites5 = xCC[2]
				xCites5 + "article:5"
				xCC[2] = xCites5
				tArt5 = " [Art. 5 organizational_sovereignty]"
			end
		end
		CtSetCode(xCC[1], xCC[2])
		if Len(xKd) >= 5
			for i = 1 to Len(xKd[5])
				if xKd[5][i][1] = xSeat[1] return CtFill(xKd[5][i][2], xDecl, tValue) + tArt5 end
			end
		end
		tMsg = CtRefusalMessage("dangling_reference")
		tOut = xDecl[2] + " " + tClause + " '" + tValue + "', which resolves to nothing: no such " + xK[1]
		if tMsg != "" tOut += " -- " + tMsg end
		return tOut + tArt5
	end
	return ""
end
# a clause's value against its seat: scalars directly, lists item by item; a
# UNION seat is checked as the alternative whose shape the value has (v0.3)
# v0.8: a word against a UNION of declarations -- it resolves to a declaration
# of one of the union's kinds, or the union's own MESSAGE speaks
func CtCheckUnionWord(xDecl, xSeat, tValue)
	xU = CtUnionByName(xSeat[2])
	if IsEmpty(xU) return "" end
	vVerbs = []
	for i = 1 to Len(xU[2])
		if xU[2][i][3] != "decl" loop end
		xK = CtKindByDeclName(xU[2][i][1])
		if IsEmpty(xK) loop end
		vVerbs + xK[1]
		for j = 1 to Len($xCondDecls)
			if $xCondDecls[j][1] = xK[1] and $xCondDecls[j][2] = tValue return "" end
		end
	end
	tMsg = xU[3]
	if tMsg = "" tMsg = "{VERB} {name} " + Upper(xSeat[1]) + " '{value}', which resolves to nothing: no such " + CtJoin(vVerbs, " or ") end
	tOwn = ""
	if Len(xU) >= 4 tOwn = xU[4] end
	xCC = CtElementCites(tOwn, "UNION", xU[1], xU, 5)
	CtSetCode(xCC[1], xCC[2])
	return CtFill(tMsg, xDecl, tValue)
end
func CtCheckSeatValue(xDecl, xSeat, xClause, bRefs)
	if CtTypeKind(xSeat) = "union" and not xSeat[3]
		xAlt = CtUnionAlt(xSeat, xClause)
		if IsEmpty(xAlt) return "" end
		if xAlt[3] = "decl"
			if not bRefs return "" end
			if xClause[3][1] != "word" return "" end
			return CtCheckUnionWord(xDecl, xSeat, xClause[3][2])
		end
		if bRefs return "" end
		return CtCheckSeatValue(xDecl, [xSeat[1], xAlt[1], xAlt[2], xSeat[4], xAlt[3]], xClause, bRefs)
	end
	tShape = xClause[3][1]
	if tShape = "word" or tShape = "string" or tShape = "number"
		return CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xSeat, xClause[3][2])
	end
	tK = CtTypeKind(xSeat)
	xItems = xClause[3][2]
	if xSeat[3] and tK = "union"
		# v0.9: a list of references to several kinds
		xKind = CtKindByVerb(xDecl[1])
		tMsgL = CtMessageFor(xKind, xSeat[1])
		for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
			tWhy = CtCheckUnionWord(xDecl, xSeat, xItems[i])
			if tWhy != ""
				if tMsgL != "" return CtFill(tMsgL, xDecl, xItems[i]) end
				return tWhy
			end
		end
		return ""
	end
	if tShape = "pairlist"
		# v0.6: each pair's value takes the form's second seat's type; v0.8: a
		# key is a name (once), a MENU word (a sequence, keys may repeat) or a
		# declaration (resolved), and a value may be a reference
		xF = CtFormByName(xSeat[2])
		if IsEmpty(xF) or Len(xF[2]) < 2 return "" end
		xKeySeat = xF[2][1]
		xValSeat = xF[2][2]
		tKeyK = CtTypeKind(xKeySeat)
		tValK = CtTypeKind(xValSeat)
		xKind = CtKindByVerb(xDecl[1])
		tMsgL = CtMessageFor(xKind, xSeat[1])
		if not bRefs
			if tKeyK != "menu"
				for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
					for j = 1 to i - 1
						if xItems[j][1] = xItems[i][1]
							CtSetCode("PARSE", [])
							return "'" + xItems[i][1] + "' is named twice in " + Upper(xSeat[1]) + " of " + xDecl[1] + " " + xDecl[2]
						end
					end
				end
			else
				for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
					tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xKeySeat, xItems[i][1])
					if tWhy != "" return tWhy end
				end
			end
			if tValK != "decl" and tValK != "union"
				for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
					tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xValSeat, xItems[i][2])
					if tWhy != "" return tWhy end
				end
			end
			# v0.27: a mark after a value is a word of the form's third seat's MENU
			for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
				if Len(xItems[i]) >= 4 and xItems[i][4] != ""
					if Len(xF[2]) < 3
						CtSetCode("PARSE", [])
						return "'" + xItems[i][4] + "' marks '" + xItems[i][1] + "' in " + Upper(xSeat[1]) + " of " + xDecl[1] + " " + xDecl[2] + ", and the form takes no mark"
					end
					tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xF[2][3], xItems[i][4])
					if tWhy != "" return tWhy end
				end
			end
			return ""
		end
		if tKeyK = "decl"
			for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
				tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xKeySeat, xItems[i][1])
				if tWhy != ""
					if tMsgL != "" return CtFill(tMsgL, xDecl, xItems[i][1]) end
					return tWhy
				end
			end
		end
		if tValK = "decl"
			for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
				tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xValSeat, xItems[i][2])
				if tWhy != ""
					if tMsgL != "" return CtFill(tMsgL, xDecl, xItems[i][2]) end
					return tWhy
				end
			end
		elseif tValK = "union"
			for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
				tWhy = CtCheckUnionWord(xDecl, xValSeat, xItems[i][2])
				if tWhy != "" return tWhy end
			end
		end
		return ""
	end
	if tK = "menu" or tK = "decl"
		for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
			tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xSeat, xItems[i])
			if tWhy != "" return tWhy end
		end
	elseif tK = "form"
		# a form's one seat may be a FORMAT: each item takes its shape
		xF = CtFormByName(xSeat[2])
		if not IsEmpty(xF) and Len(xF[2]) > 0 and CtTypeKind(xF[2][1]) = "format"
			for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
				tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xF[2][1], xItems[i])
				if tWhy != "" return tWhy end
			end
		end
	end
	return ""
end
# ---- the printed verdict -----------------------------------------------------

func CtPrintVerdict(xDecls)
	? "ok"
	xFirst = xDecls[1]
	? "name " + xFirst[2]
	? "rationale " + xFirst[5]
	xC = xFirst[4]
	for i = 1 to Len(xC)
		if xC[i][3][1] = "word" or xC[i][3][1] = "string" or xC[i][3][1] = "number"
			? Lower(xC[i][1]) + " " + xC[i][3][2]
		end
	end
	xV = CtVerbs()
	for i = 1 to Len(xV)
		nN = 0
		for j = 1 to Len(xDecls)
			if xDecls[j][1] = xV[i] nN++ end
		end
		? "count " + String(xV[i]) + " " + String(nN)
	end
	# v0.27: the fields the sentence marks personal or confidential, in the order written
	xMk = CtMarkedFields(xDecls)
	if Len(xMk) > 0 ? "personal " + CtJoin(xMk, ", ") end
end
# ---- v0.27: the marks and the safeguards -------------------------------------------
# $aCourtMarks holds [kind, seat, markSeat] paths from the CONSTITUTION's three-part PERSONAL paths; a
# field whose mark reads personal or confidential is a personal datum at the record level (stzFieldTags'
# two tags). $aCourtSafeguards holds [path, word]: the ask under anonymisation answers redacted, under
# consent whole; the voice under redaction tells its rows redacted.
func CtMarkedFields(xDecls)
	xOut = []
	for m = 1 to Len($vCourtMarks)
		xKind = ""
		for k = 1 to Len($xCourtKinds)
			if $xCourtKinds[k][2] = $vCourtMarks[m][1] xKind = $xCourtKinds[k] end
		end
		if IsEmpty(xKind) loop end
		for d = 1 to Len(xDecls)
			if xDecls[d][1] != xKind[1] loop end
			xC = xDecls[d][4]
			for c = 1 to Len(xC)
				if Lower(xC[c][1]) != $vCourtMarks[m][2] loop end
				if xC[c][3][1] != "pairlist" loop end
				xItems = xC[c][3][2]
				for i = 1 to Len(xItems)
					if Len(xItems[i]) >= 4 and (xItems[i][4] = "personal" or xItems[i][4] = "confidential")
						if not CtInList(xItems[i][1], xOut) xOut + xItems[i][1] end
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end
	return xOut
end
func CtSafeguard(tPath)
	for i = 1 to Len($vCourtSafeguards)
		if $vCourtSafeguards[i][1] = tPath return $vCourtSafeguards[i][2] end
	end
	return ""
end
# a copy of the rows (JSON objects: the mark, then [key, value] pairs) with each marked field's value [personal]
func CtRedactRows(xRows, xFields)
	if Len(xFields) = 0 return xRows end
	xOut = []
	for i = 1 to Len(xRows)
		vRow = []
		for j = 1 to Len(xRows[i])
			xV = xRows[i][j]
			if j > 1 and IsList(xV) and Len(xV) = 2 and IsString(xV[1]) and CtInList(xV[1], xFields)
				vRow + [xV[1], "[personal]"]
			else
				vRow + xV
			end
		end
		xOut + vRow
	end
	return xOut
end
# ---- the refinement gate ------------------------------------------------------
# `<court>.ring refine <file> <file.rfn>`: one refinement, judged by the
# five stages before it lands (charter section 6; stzRefinableCode.ring's
# order): structural -- the refined text is a sentence of the language;
# constraint -- the point exists, FROM is its value, TO has the seat's
# shape; derivation -- the whole file still holds (one namespace, required
# seats); governance -- an author and a reason are named; trust -- the
# proposal's posture reaches the point's floor. Admitted, the refined text
# is written to <file>.refined and the inverse to <file>.revert.rfn; the
# refusal is one human line and one C2 record (JSON) beneath it.

func CtJson(tS)
	tOut = ""
	for i = 1 to Len(tS)
		tC = tS[i]
		if tC = '"' or tC = Char(92)
			tOut += Char(92) + tC
		elseif tC = Char(10)
			tOut += Char(92) + "n"
		else
			tOut += tC
		end
	end
	return '"' + tOut + '"'
end
func CtRecord(tCode, tMsg, tFile, nLine, xCites, tWhy, tTodo)
	tC = ""
	for i = 1 to Len(xCites)
		if i > 1 tC += ", " end
		tC += CtJson(xCites[i])
	end
	return '{"code": ' + CtJson(tCode) + ', "severity": "error", "message": ' + CtJson(tMsg) +
	       ', "span": {"file": ' + CtJson(tFile) + ', "line": ' + String(nLine) + '}, "cites": [' + tC + ']' +
	       ', "language": ' + CtJson($tCourtLang) + ', "why": ' + CtJson(tWhy) + ', "todo": ' + CtJson(tTodo) + '}'
end
func CtPostureRank(tP)
	if tP = "trusted" return 3 end
	if tP = "external" return 2 end
	if tP = "sandboxed" return 1 end
	if tP = "llm" return 0 end
	return -1
end
# the refinement sentence's own tables (rfn.haro), read by the same parser
func CtRfnKinds
	return [ ["REFINE", "refinement", [ ["target", "text", false, false], ["kind", "name", false, false], ["from", "text", false, false],
	          ["to", "text", false, false], ["author", "text", false, false], ["posture", "name", false, false], ["reason", "text", false, false] ]] ]
end
func CtClauseText(xDecl, tClause)
	xC = xDecl[4]
	for i = 1 to Len(xC)
		if xC[i][1] = tClause return xC[i][3][2] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtRefuse(tStage, tCode, tMsg, tFile, nLine, xCites, tWhy, tTodo)
	? $tCourtLang + " (line " + String(nLine) + "): " + tStage + ": " + tMsg
	? CtRecord(tCode, tStage + ": " + tMsg, tFile, nLine, xCites, tWhy, tTodo)
	CtAuditWrite("refused", tStage, tCode)
end
func CtRefine(tFile, tRfnFile)
	tSrc = Read(tFile)
	tRfn = Read(tRfnFile)

	# the refinement sentence, parsed by this court with the rfn tables
	xSaveKinds = $xCourtKinds
	xSaveLang = $tCourtLang
	$xCourtKinds = CtRfnKinds()
	$tCourtLang = "rfn"
	xR = ""
	tErr = ""
	try
		xRs = CtDeclare(tRfn)
		xR = xRs[1]
	catch
		tErr = cCatchError
	end
	$xCourtKinds = xSaveKinds
	$tCourtLang = xSaveLang
	if not IsEmpty(tErr) and tErr != ""
		? tErr
		return
	end
	tTarget = CtClauseText(xR, "TARGET")
	tFrom = CtClauseText(xR, "FROM")
	tTo = CtClauseText(xR, "TO")
	tAuthor = CtClauseText(xR, "AUTHOR")
	tPosture = CtClauseText(xR, "POSTURE")
	tReason = CtClauseText(xR, "REASON")
	nRLine = xR[3]
	# v0.24: under visible_state every event of this proposal joins the sentence's audit chain
	$tCourtAuditFile = ""
	if CtUnderArticle("visible_state")
		$tCourtAuditFile = tFile + ".audit"
		$vCourtAuditProposal = [xR[2], tTarget, tFrom, tTo, tAuthor, tPosture]
	end

	# structural, on the ORIGINAL: the file must be a sentence before it is refined
	xDecls = ""
	try
		xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
	catch
		CtRefuse("structural", "NOT_A_SENTENCE", cCatchError, tFile, 1, ["rule:structural"],
		         "the gate's structural stage is the language's own court, and the file to refine is not a sentence of it",
		         "make the file a sentence of the language first; then propose the refinement")
		return
	end

	# constraint: the point exists, FROM is its value, TO fits the seat
	nDot = SubStr(tTarget, ".")
	if nDot = 0
		CtRefuse("constraint", "NO_SUCH_POINT", "the target '" + tTarget + "' is not declaration.CLAUSE", tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         ["rule:constraint"], "a point is a clause of a declaration, named declaration.CLAUSE", "name the point as <declaration>.<CLAUSE>")
		return
	end
	tDeclName = Left(tTarget, nDot - 1)
	tClause = SubStr(tTarget, nDot + 1)
	xDecl = ""
	for i = 1 to Len(xDecls)
		if xDecls[i][2] = tDeclName xDecl = xDecls[i] end
	end
	if IsEmpty(xDecl)
		CtRefuse("constraint", "NO_SUCH_POINT", "no declaration '" + tDeclName + "' in " + tFile, tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         ["rule:constraint"], "every named thing is a refinement point, and nothing by this name is declared", "name a declaration the file carries")
		return
	end
	xKind = CtKindByVerb(xDecl[1])
	xSeat = CtSeatByClause(xKind, tClause)
	if IsEmpty(xSeat)
		CtRefuse("constraint", "NO_SUCH_POINT", xDecl[1] + " has no clause " + tClause + "; allowed are " + CtJoin(CtAllowedClauses(xKind), ", "),
		         tRfnFile, nRLine, ["rule:constraint"], "the point's clause is not a seat of its declaration kind", "name one of the allowed clauses")
		return
	end
	tShape = CtClauseShape(xSeat)
	if tShape = "union"
		# a UNION seat's shape is the shape of the value written (v0.3)
		tShape = "word"
		xCw = xDecl[4]
		for i = 1 to Len(xCw)
			if xCw[i][1] = tClause tShape = xCw[i][3][1] end
		end
	end
	if tShape != "word" and tShape != "string" and tShape != "number"
		CtRefuse("constraint", "NOT_A_KNOB", tClause + " is a list seat; this gate refines scalar points only", tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         ["rule:constraint"], "the spike's gate refines knobs, fields and symbols, not composites", "refine a scalar clause")
		return
	end
	# v0.2: the point is declared in REFINE's POINTS, with its kind. A language
	# that declares no REFINE at all keeps the spike's first rule: every
	# scalar seat is a point (a word or number a knob, a text a field) at the
	# court's floor, trusted.
	tPointName = xKind[2] + "." + Lower(tClause)
	# v0.25: the chain learns the point, so a personal point's values are redacted in it
	if $tCourtAuditFile != "" $vCourtAuditProposal + tPointName end
	tDeclaredKind = ""
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtPoints)
		if $xCourtPoints[i][1] = tPointName tDeclaredKind = $xCourtPoints[i][2] end
	end
	if Len($xCourtPoints) = 0
		tDeclaredKind = "field"
		if tShape = "word" or tShape = "number" tDeclaredKind = "knob" end
	end
	if tDeclaredKind = ""
		CtRefuse("constraint", "NOT_A_POINT", "'" + tTarget + "' is not a declared refinement point of " + $tCourtLang + " (" + tPointName + " is not in REFINE's POINTS)",
		         tRfnFile, nRLine, ["rule:refine-points"], "every refinable point is declared by the language, with its kind; the boundaries are language-required, not author-chosen",
		         "propose a change to a declared point, or declare this one in the language's REFINE")
		return
	end
	tKindGiven = CtClauseText(xR, "KIND")
	if tKindGiven != tDeclaredKind
		CtRefuse("constraint", "KIND_MISMATCH", "'" + tTarget + "' is a " + tDeclaredKind + ", not a " + tKindGiven, tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         ["rule:refine-points"], "the point's kind is declared by the language", "say KIND " + tDeclaredKind)
		return
	end
	# the clause as written, with its token span
	xClause = ""
	xC = xDecl[4]
	for i = 1 to Len(xC)
		if xC[i][1] = tClause xClause = xC[i] end
	end
	if IsEmpty(xClause)
		CtRefuse("constraint", "POINT_UNSET", xDecl[1] + " " + tDeclName + " does not write " + tClause + "; this gate refines a clause that is written",
		         tRfnFile, nRLine, ["rule:constraint"], "a refinement changes a value the sentence carries", "write the clause first, then refine it")
		return
	end
	tCurrent = xClause[3][2]
	if tCurrent != tFrom
		CtRefuse("constraint", "FROM_MISMATCH", tClause + " of " + tDeclName + " is '" + tCurrent + "', not '" + tFrom + "'", tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         ["rule:constraint"], "FROM is an assertion about the point's value, and it does not hold", "state the value the file carries")
		return
	end
	if tShape = "number"
		for i = 1 to Len(tTo)
			if not CtIsDigit(tTo[i])
				CtRefuse("constraint", "SHAPE", tClause + " takes a number, and '" + tTo + "' is not one", tRfnFile, nRLine,
				         ["rule:constraint"], "the seat's shape is declared", "propose a number")
				return
			end
		end
	elseif tShape = "word"
		for i = 1 to Len(tTo)
			if not CtIsLowerish(tTo[i])
				CtRefuse("constraint", "SHAPE", tClause + " takes a word, and '" + tTo + "' is not lower_snake", tRfnFile, nRLine,
				         ["rule:constraint"], "the seat's shape is declared", "propose a lower_snake word")
				return
			end
		end
	end
	# v0.2: the bounds of the point are the seat's declared type (a MENU, a RANGE, a FORMAT)
	tWhy = CtCheckScalar(xDecl, xSeat, tTo)
	if tWhy != ""
		CtRefuse("constraint", "OUT_OF_BOUNDS", tWhy, tRfnFile, nRLine, ["rule:constraint"],
		         "a knob's bounds are the declared type of its seat; the court speaks the type's own message",
		         "propose a value the seat's type admits")
		return
	end

	# the refined text: the value's span replaced, nothing else touched
	nStart = xClause[4]
	nEnd = xClause[5]
	tNew = tTo
	if tShape = "string" tNew = '"' + tTo + '"' end
	tRefined = Left(tSrc, nStart - 1) + tNew + SubStr(tSrc, nEnd)

	# derivation: the whole file still holds (the court's checks on the refined text)
	try
		CtDeclare(tRefined)
	catch
		CtRefuse("derivation", "DERIVATION", cCatchError, tFile, xClause[2], ["rule:derivation"],
		         "the refined sentence breaks a rule of the language", "choose a value the language admits")
		return
	end

	# governance: an author and a reason
	if tAuthor = "" or tReason = ""
		CtRefuse("governance", "UNATTRIBUTED", "a refinement names its author and its reason; this one does not", tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         ["rule:governance"], "the audit chain is author, authority, rule, verdict, and an unattributed change has no chain", "name the author and the reason")
		return
	end

	# trust: the point's floor (this court: trusted for every point) against the posture
	nRank = CtPostureRank(tPosture)
	if nRank < 0
		CtRefuse("trust", "POSTURE", "'" + tPosture + "' is not a posture: trusted, external, sandboxed or llm", tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         ["rule:trust"], "the trust ladder is closed", "name one of the four postures")
		return
	end
	# v0.2: the floor is the point's own (REFINE's FLOOR), trusted when it declares none
	tFloor = "trusted"
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtFloors)
		if $xCourtFloors[i][1] = tPointName tFloor = $xCourtFloors[i][2] end
	end
	if nRank < CtPostureRank(tFloor)
		tMsgT = "posture :" + tPosture + " below the required floor :" + tFloor + " for '" + tTarget + "'"
		vCitesT = ["rule:trust-floor"]
		# v0.23: under trust_hierarchy the refusal names its article and cites it
		if CtUnderArticle("trust_hierarchy")
			tMsgT += " [Art. 6 trust_hierarchy]"
			vCitesT + "article:6"
		end
		CtRefuse("trust", "TRUST_FLOOR", tMsgT, tRfnFile, nRLine,
		         vCitesT, "the point's floor is declared by the language (REFINE's FLOOR; trusted when none is declared): a proposal below it is refused by construction, not by convention",
		         "an actor of posture :" + tFloor + " or above may propose the same change; or lower the point's floor in the language's REFINE")
		return
	end

	# admitted: the refined text, and its inverse, written beside the file
	Write(tFile + ".refined", tRefined)
	tRevert = "DEFINE REFINE revert_of_" + xR[2] + " AS (" + Char(10) +
	          '  TARGET "' + tTarget + '", KIND ' + CtClauseText(xR, "KIND") + ',' + Char(10) +
	          '  FROM "' + tTo + '", TO "' + tFrom + '",' + Char(10) +
	          '  AUTHOR "' + tAuthor + '", POSTURE ' + tPosture + ',' + Char(10) +
	          '  REASON "the inverse of ' + xR[2] + ', computed before it landed"' + Char(10) +
	          ') RATIONALE "A revert is its own event; nothing is erased"' + Char(10)
	Write(tFile + ".revert.rfn", tRevert)
	# v0.25: a personal point's values are not spoken (W4.4); the inverse beside the file keeps them, as the file does
	tShownA = tFrom + " -> " + tTo
	if CtIsPersonal(tPointName) tShownA = "[personal] -> [personal]" end
	? "admitted: " + tTarget + " " + tShownA + " [" + tPosture + "] (structural + constraint + derivation + governance + trust passed); inverse in " + tFile + ".revert.rfn"
	CtAuditWrite("admitted", "", "")
end
# ---- v0.6: a sentence's expressions evaluated, and a WALK run ---------------------
# `<court>.ring eval <file> <decl> <seat> <json>`: the expression in SEAT of the
# declaration DECL, evaluated on the record, answers true or false.
# `<court>.ring walk <file> <name> <json>`: the record walks the steps of the
# declaration NAME under the WALK of its kind -- every step whose THROUGH seat
# names it, in ORDER; at each step the FORMULA, when written, computes the
# COMPUTE seat's value into the record first (for this step's guards and every
# later one, as zing's runner does), then each GUARD in the WALK's order must
# hold; the first that does not stops the walk. The verdict is JSON:
#   {"status": "complete", "computed": {name: value, ...}}
#   {"status": "failed", "at": step, "code": <the FAIL seat>, "reason": why}
# A guard read through a reference (enforcing.rule) takes its reason from the
# referenced declaration's `message` seat when it has one.

func CtDeclNamed(xDecls, tName)
	for i = 1 to Len(xDecls)
		if xDecls[i][2] = tName return xDecls[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
func CtWalkOf(tKindName)
	for i = 1 to Len($xCourtWalks)
		if $xCourtWalks[i][2] = tKindName return $xCourtWalks[i] end
	end
	return ""
end
# the node of an expression seat, parsed under its language; NULL when the
# clause is not written
func CtExprNode(xDecl, tSeat)
	xKind = CtKindByVerb(xDecl[1])
	xSeat = CtSeatByClause(xKind, Upper(tSeat))
	if IsEmpty(xSeat) Raise("no seat '" + tSeat + "' on " + xDecl[1]) end
	if CtTypeKind(xSeat) != "expr" Raise(Upper(tSeat) + " of " + xDecl[1] + " " + xDecl[2] + " is not an expression seat") end
	tText = CondScalar(xDecl, tSeat)
	if IsEmpty(tText) return "" end
	xE = CtExprByName(xSeat[2])
	if IsEmpty(xE) Raise("the court carries no EXPRESSION called '" + xSeat[2] + "'") end
	CtExprUse(xE)
	return ExParse(tText, [])
end
func CtEval(xDecls, tDecl, tSeat, xRecord)
	xD = CtDeclNamed(xDecls, tDecl)
	if IsEmpty(xD) Raise("no declaration named '" + tDecl + "' in this file") end
	xNode = CtExprNode(xD, tSeat)
	if IsEmpty(xNode) Raise(Upper(tSeat) + " is not written on " + xD[1] + " " + xD[2]) end
	ExSetRecord(xRecord)
	return ExBool(xNode, [])
end
# a guard of a step: [node, reason], or [NULL, ""] when the seat is not written
func CtGuard(xDecls, xStep, tPath)
	nDot = SubStr(tPath, ".")
	if nDot = 0
		xNode = CtExprNode(xStep, tPath)
		return [xNode, Upper(tPath) + " failed"]
	end
	tHead = Left(tPath, nDot - 1)
	tTail = SubStr(tPath, nDot + 1)
	tRef = CondScalar(xStep, tHead)
	if IsEmpty(tRef) return ["", ""] end
	xTarget = CtDeclNamed(xDecls, tRef)
	if IsEmpty(xTarget) return ["", ""] end
	xNode = CtExprNode(xTarget, tTail)
	tReason = CondScalar(xTarget, "message")
	if IsEmpty(tReason) tReason = Upper(tTail) + " of " + xTarget[1] + " " + xTarget[2] + " failed" end
	return [xNode, tReason]
end
func CtWalk(xDecls, tName, xRecord)
	xD = CtDeclNamed(xDecls, tName)
	if IsEmpty(xD) Raise("no declaration named '" + tName + "' in this file") end
	xKind = CtKindByVerb(xD[1])
	xW = CtWalkOf(xKind[2])
	if IsEmpty(xW) Raise("no WALK of " + xKind[2] + " is declared, so " + xD[1] + " " + tName + " cannot be walked") end
	xStepKind = CtKindByDeclName(xW[3])
	# the steps THROUGH this declaration, in ORDER (an insertion sort on the
	# number: Ring's sort() orders a column of text)
	xSteps = []
	for i = 1 to Len(xDecls)
		if xDecls[i][1] != xStepKind[1] loop end
		tThrough = CondScalar(xDecls[i], xW[4])
		if IsEmpty(tThrough) or tThrough != tName loop end
		nOrder = Number(CondScalar(xDecls[i], xW[5]))
		nAt = Len(xSteps) + 1
		for j = 1 to Len(xSteps)
			if nOrder < xSteps[j][1]
				nAt = j
				exit
			end
		end
		xEntry = [nOrder, xDecls[i]]
		if nAt > Len(xSteps)
			xSteps + xEntry
		else
			# Ring's insert() puts the item AFTER the index: before j is after j-1 (HF-52)
			Insert(xSteps, nAt - 1, xEntry)
		end
	end
	ExSetRecord(xRecord)
	vComputed = [ExObjMark()]
	for i = 1 to Len(xSteps)
		xStep = xSteps[i][2]
		if xW[7] != "" and xW[8] != ""
			tTarget = CondScalar(xStep, xW[7])
			xF = CtExprNode(xStep, xW[8])
			if not IsEmpty(tTarget) and not IsEmpty(xF)
				xV = ExNum(ExEval(xF, []))
				$vExprOverlay + [tTarget, xV]
				vPair = [tTarget, xV]
				vComputed + vPair
			end
		end
		xG = xW[6]
		for j = 1 to Len(xG)
			xGuard = CtGuard(xDecls, xStep, xG[j])
			if IsEmpty(xGuard[1]) loop end
			if not ExBool(xGuard[1], [])
				xOut = [ExObjMark(), ["status", "failed"], ["at", xStep[2]]]
				if xW[9] != ""
					tCode = CondScalar(xStep, xW[9])
					if not IsEmpty(tCode)
						vPair = ["code", tCode]
						xOut + vPair
					end
				end
				vPair = ["reason", xGuard[2]]
				xOut + vPair
				return xOut
			end
		end
	end
	xOut = [ExObjMark(), ["status", "complete"], ["computed", vComputed]]
	return xOut
end
# the command: check <file> | refine <file> <file.rfn> | eval ... | walk ... | ask ...
func CtMain
	if Len(sysargv) < 4
		? "usage: <court>.haro check <file" + $tCourtExt + "> | refine <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <file.rfn> | eval <file> <decl> <seat> <json> | walk <file> <name> <json> | ask <file> <question> <rows json> | audit <file>"
		return
	end
	tVerb = sysargv[3]
	# the judged file's folder: a SENTENCE seat's file is read beside it (v0.4)
	$tCourtDir = CtDirOf(sysargv[4])
	if tVerb = "check"
		# v0.10: `check <file> [<world.json>]` -- with a world, every SYMBOL seat
		# resolves against it; without one, a sentence that holds SYMBOL seats is
		# judged alone and the last line says so, a warning (C2's "undecidable
		# without more input"), never a refusal
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			# v0.17: `surfaces` asks each surface's own court to judge its queries (a language that is understood)
			if not IsEmpty($xCourtUnderstand) and Len(sysargv) >= 5
				if sysargv[5] = "surfaces" $bNSurfaces = true end
			end
			if Len(sysargv) >= 5 and not $bNSurfaces $xCourtWorldFile = CtWorldLoad(sysargv[5]) end
			$vCourtWarnings = []
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			CtPrintVerdict(xDecls)
			# v0.25: a CONSTRAINT of SEVERITY warning is spoken after the verdict, with its code and line
			for i = 1 to Len($vCourtWarnings)
				? "warning " + String($vCourtWarnings[i][1]) + ": " + String($vCourtWarnings[i][4]) + " (line " + String($vCourtWarnings[i][3]) + ")"
			end
			if IsEmpty($xCourtWorldFile) and Len($xCourtSymbols) > 0
				nSites = Len(CtSymbolSites(xDecls))
				if nSites > 0
					? "warning NO_WORLD: no world to resolve against; " + String(nSites) + " symbol reference(s) unresolved, which is what C3 section 3.2 asks a project to close"
				end
			end
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "diagnose"
		# v0.11: the same court, in the family's machine form (C2 v1.2.0)
		tWorldPath = ""
		if not IsEmpty($xCourtUnderstand) and Len(sysargv) >= 5
			if sysargv[5] = "surfaces" $bNSurfaces = true end
		end
		if Len(sysargv) >= 5 and not $bNSurfaces tWorldPath = sysargv[5] end
		? CtDiagnosticsJson(CtDiagnose(sysargv[4], tWorldPath))
	elseif tVerb = "world"
		# v0.10: the sentence's own C1 rows, as JSON
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			xWRows = CtWorldRows(xDecls, CtWorldStem(sysargv[4]) + $tCourtExt)
			# v0.40: the doors each declaration opens, published for the consumer that enforces them -- only where the language NEEDS (D51)
			xEW = CtLangEntry($tCourtLang)
			if not IsEmpty(xEW)
				if Len(xEW) >= 25 xWRows + ["opens", NdRows(xDecls, xEW[25], CtWorldStem(sysargv[4]) + $tCourtExt)] end
			end
			? ExJson(xWRows)
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "refine"
		if Len(sysargv) < 5
			? "usage: <court>.haro refine <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <file.rfn>"
			return
		end
		CtRefine(sysargv[4], sysargv[5])
	elseif tVerb = "audit"
		# v0.24: the audit chain of a sentence under visible_state, answered as a query: every
		# refinement event kept beside the sentence, in order, then their count
		tAuditPath = sysargv[4] + ".audit"
		if not CtUnderArticle("visible_state")
			? "no audit chain: " + $tCourtLang + " is under no visible_state"
		elseif not FExists(tAuditPath)
			? "no audit chain yet: " + tAuditPath + " does not exist"
		else
			tAuditText = Read(tAuditPath)
			nAuditEvents = 0
			tAuditLine = ""
			for i = 1 to Len(tAuditText)
				if tAuditText[i] = Char(10)
					if tAuditLine != ""
						? tAuditLine
						nAuditEvents++
					end
					tAuditLine = ""
				else
					tAuditLine += tAuditText[i]
				end
			end
			? String(nAuditEvents) + " events"
		end
	elseif tVerb = "eval"
		if Len(sysargv) < 7
			? "usage: <court>.haro eval <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <decl> <seat> <json>"
			return
		end
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			xRecord = ExJsonParse(sysargv[7])
			if CtEval(xDecls, sysargv[5], sysargv[6], xRecord)
				? "true"
			else
				? "false"
			end
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "walk"
		if Len(sysargv) < 6
			? "usage: <court>.haro walk <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <name> <json>"
			return
		end
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			xRecord = ExJsonParse(sysargv[6])
			? ExJson(CtWalk(xDecls, sysargv[5], xRecord))
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "run"
		# v0.9: an algorithm run on a record
		if Len(sysargv) < 6
			? "usage: <court>.haro run <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <algorithm> <record json>"
			return
		end
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			if IsEmpty($xCourtRun) CtFail(1, "this language declares no RUN, so nothing in it runs") end
			xRecord = ExJsonParse(sysargv[6])
			? ExJson(RunAlgorithm(xDecls, sysargv[5], xRecord))
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "narrate"
		# v0.13: the sentence narrated back in the language's own voice, on stdout, never stored
		if Len(sysargv) < 4
			? "usage: <court>.haro narrate <file" + $tCourtExt + ">"
			return
		end
		try
			if IsEmpty($xCourtNarrate) CtFail(1, "this language declares no NARRATE, so it has no voice") end
			NarrateRun(sysargv[4])
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "narrate-run"
		# v0.16: an algorithm run on a record, told in the language's own voice -- the same run `run` makes, never a second one
		if Len(sysargv) < 6
			? "usage: <court>.haro narrate-run <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <algorithm> <record json>"
			return
		end
		try
			if IsEmpty($xCourtNarrate) CtFail(1, "this language declares no NARRATE, so it has no voice") end
			if IsEmpty($xCourtRun) CtFail(1, "this language declares no RUN, so nothing in it runs") end
			NarTellRun(sysargv[4], sysargv[5], sysargv[6])
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "narrate-ask"
		# v0.16: a question answered on rows, told in the language's own voice -- the same answer `ask` gives
		if Len(sysargv) < 6
			? "usage: <court>.haro narrate-ask <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <question> <rows json>"
			return
		end
		try
			if IsEmpty($xCourtNarrate) CtFail(1, "this language declares no NARRATE, so it has no voice") end
			if IsEmpty($xCourtAsk) CtFail(1, "this language declares no ASK, so it answers no question") end
			NarTellAsk(sysargv[4], sysargv[5], sysargv[6])
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "family"
		# v0.12: the members of every declared family, generated from the FORMS
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			if IsEmpty($xCourtFormset) CtFail(1, "this language declares no FORMS, so it spells no family") end
			FormsPrintFamilies(xDecls)
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif tVerb = "spellings"
		# v0.12: a list of names judged against the FORMS and the declared families
		if Len(sysargv) < 5
			? "usage: <court>.haro spellings <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <names.txt>"
			return
		end
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			if IsEmpty($xCourtFormset) CtFail(1, "this language declares no FORMS, so it judges no spelling") end
			FormsPrintSpellings(xDecls, FormsReadNames(sysargv[5]))
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	elseif not IsEmpty($xCourtUnderstand) and CtInList(tVerb, ["tokens", "understand", "ask", "vocabulary", "examples"])
		# v0.17: a human language over a declared world, understood (n_lib.haro); `ask` here takes a tongue and
		# a text, where the Q letter's takes a question and rows -- different courts, different arguments
		NatMain(tVerb)
	elseif tVerb = "ask"
		# v0.7: a question of the declared world, answered on the rows handed in
		if Len(sysargv) < 6
			? "usage: <court>.haro ask <file" + $tCourtExt + "> <question> <rows json>"
			return
		end
		tSrc = Read(sysargv[4])
		try
			xDecls = CtDeclare(tSrc)
			if IsEmpty($xCourtAsk) CtFail(1, "this language declares no ASK, so it answers no question") end
			xRows = ExJsonParse(sysargv[6])
			xAns = AskRun(xDecls, sysargv[5], xRows)
			# v0.27: under anonymisation the ask path answers with the marked fields redacted; under consent, whole
			if CtSafeguard("ask") = "anonymisation" xAns = CtRedactRows(xAns, CtMarkedFields(xDecls)) end
			? ExJson(xAns)
		catch
			? cCatchError
		end
	else
		? "unknown verb '" + tVerb + "'; this court answers: check, refine, eval, walk, ask, run, world, diagnose, family, spellings, narrate, narrate-run, narrate-ask, audit"
	end
end
